    "result_text": "I've added corrections, and all 4 Playwright tests in `bin/e2e` pass, including the audit lines they check.\n\n**How it behaves**\n- **Corrects field:** the claim form has a new \"Corrects claim #\" box (`claim-form-corrects`). A claim with a negative amount is refused unless that box names the number of a settled claim belonging to the same person. Each claim row shows the number it corrects (`claim-corrects`), left blank for ordinary claims.\n- **Two extra refusals:** a positive claim that fills in the box is refused, since only a negative amount can correct something. A negative amount through the quick-add bar is always refused, because that bar has no way to name a claim.\n- **Due:** a correction's due is its amount times the rate, rounded half to even the same way as other claims. The floor and the late charge are skipped. This holds everywhere a due is worked out: on screen, in the totals, when settling and in statements.\n- **Everything else** works as for any claim: corrections get numbers, are opened and settled, and count in every total. The audit lines are unchanged.\n\n**Changes**\n- **Database:** a new migration, `src/main/java/db/migration/V20__claim_correction.java`, adds a `corrects` column to claims. It also removes the old rule that an amount can't be negative. That rule had no name in the database, so the migration has to look it up while running, which is why it's written in Java rather than plain SQL. It removes only the amount rule; the status rule is untouched.\n- **Server:** the form check now accepts negative amounts but requires a claim number with them. A new step, `CheckClaimAddCorrection` / `CheckClaimEditCorrection`, confirms that number is a settled claim of the same person; it runs when adding a claim and when editing one. The floor and late-charge code skips corrections.\n- **Front end:** the money helpers in `Rates.tsx` and the claimed total in `Claims.tsx` only worked for amounts of zero or more. Before this fix, `-0.30` would have come out as `0.30`, so I made them handle negative values.\n\n**Not covered by the tests**\n- **Overdue:** an open correction past its due-by date still shows `overdue = yes` and counts in the overdue numbers, just with no late charge added. The request only said there's no late charge, so I didn't change that.\n- **Edits:** editing a draft goes through the same correction check, but no test exercises it.",
